# DisciplineOS — Performance & Discipline (Portfolio Demo)

A multi-page, responsive portfolio website built to showcase clean layout, accessibility-minded UI, and “real client site” features.

---

## Pages

- **Home** (`index.html`)  
  Hero + CTAs, layered background, parallax section, embedded YouTube video, feature cards, sticky transparent navbar.

- **Training** (`training.html`)  
  Responsive **table layout** with an accessible horizontal scroll wrapper, plus program cards, and CTAs (phone/email).

- **Contact** (`contact.html`)  
  HTML5-validated contact form + CTAs (phone/email) + Google Maps embed.

---

## Key Features

### UI / UX
- Sticky **transparent navbar** with blur effect
- Mobile nav menu toggle below **500px**
- Strong CTA placement (phone + email + buttons)
- Hover effects (transform + glow) and button transitions
- Layered background with image + opacity overlays
- **Parallax** section (`background-attachment: fixed`)
- YouTube embed (`youtube-nocookie.com`)

### Accessibility (WCAG-friendly patterns)
- Skip link (“Skip to content”)
- `:focus-visible` styles for keyboard users
- Semantic sections/headings
- Form labels + required fields
- Table wrapped in a focusable scroll region for smaller screens

### Responsive Layout
- Mobile-first adjustments
- Grid collapses cleanly under 900px
- Table becomes horizontally scrollable on smaller widths

### Minimal JavaScript
Only used for:
- Theme toggle (dark/light) with `localStorage` persistence
- Mobile nav open/close
- Footer year

Everything else is handled with HTML/CSS.

---

## Tech Stack

- HTML5
- CSS3 (custom properties, responsive grid, scroll/entry animation)
- Vanilla JavaScript (tiny utility script)
- Google Fonts (Inter)
- Google Maps embed (iframe)

